{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Behold, a people like a lioness rises up.</b> This alludes that they will defeat the kings of Canaan; and more fittingly it is an allusion to the war against Midian, for no war like it was ever heard — not a single man of Israel was missing, and five kings died, and human females who had not known the lying of a male, thirty-two thousand. <b>And drinks the blood of the slain</b> — the booty and all their host." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״הן עם כלביא יקום״ — when they rise from their beds they gather strength like a lion and seize the commandments of ציצית and תפילין and the reading of קריאת שמע. And at night, ״he will not lie down״: until he eats and destroys every harmful thing that comes to devour him — how so? He reads קריאת שמע and says ״בידך אפקיד רוחי,״ and the Holy One, blessed be He, fights on his behalf. And they further interpreted ״he will not lie down until he eats prey״ as a prophecy about Moses, that he would not die until he took vengeance upon them, as it is said (Numbers 31:2): ״נקם נקמת בני ישראל מאת המדינים אחר תאסף״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:38.795728360Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}